@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Install dependencies with `pnpm install` and serve the application with `pnpm start`.
+The port defaults to `11222` and can be overridden with `PORT`.
+
+The server sends `Permissions-Policy` directives allowing this application's
+origin to request resources on the user's local network and loopback interface.
+It includes both the current `local-network` and `loopback-network` directives
+and the older `local-network-access` alias.
+
+Public deployments must use HTTPS. Users must grant any browser network access
+permission, and local services must allow the application's origin through CORS
+when requests need to read cross-origin responses. These headers do not grant
+permission on the user's behalf.
+
+If embedding this app in a cross-origin iframe, the parent must delegate
+`local-network; loopback-network; local-network-access` through the iframe's
+`allow` attribute and permit the app's origin in any parent Permissions-Policy.
+If deploying with another static host, configure that host to send the same
+Permissions-Policy header; HTML meta tags cannot replace this response header.
+
+Reference: https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/
